                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Configure delivery modes and faculty`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Turn the architecture into a deliverable design under the real constraints: only <strong>3 of 5 senior strategy faculty</strong> are free (the other two earn £0.6m on open programmes you'd cannibalise), a fixed budget, and a 10-week launch against a 16–18-week build. Set the per-learner delivery mix across in-person, virtual-live, asynchronous digital and coaching/application; place scarce faculty on the <em>2–3 highest-leverage moments only</em>; design Kirkpatrick <strong>L3/L4</strong> impact measurement in; and sequence the build — a phased proof cohort can hit the date a full bespoke build cannot.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Pitch, defend, and protect the margin`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Present to the CHRO and procurement, who push for more days, a lower price, and a faster launch. Frame the pitch on NorthGrid's <strong>business outcomes</strong>, not features. When the CHRO asks for two extra days at the same price, remember: that's 240 extra learner-days that take margin from 31% to 19% — <em>get something for what you give</em>, or hold the line. Answer the discount demand without breaking the <strong>30% floor</strong>, and offer a phased cohort-1 proof as the win-protecting move. Walk away from value-destroying concessions.`,

                    r1_need_label:          `What is NorthGrid actually buying? Name the true learning need before you design.`,
