                    insight_excellent:      `Mandate won and margin lifted: you architected a client-first hybrid solution that hit the fit, the 10-week launch and ≥38% margin. NorthGrid renews on demonstrated impact — and the anchor relationship is reinforced rather than risked.`,
                    insight_won:            `Mandate won: a fundable, well-fitted design at or above the 30% floor with a credible launch. You beat two rivals by solving NorthGrid's business problem, not by selling a course catalogue.`,
                    insight_undeliverable:  `Won on undeliverable terms: you took the bid below the MD's 30% margin floor. A win that loses money — or a rushed launch that fails cohort 1 — ends the anchor relationship and the reference. This is the win that should have been a walk-away.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `Priced out of the envelope: your design still exceeds the £1.8m budget, so the bid is unfundable however good the pedagogy. The gap closes through hybrid format and delivery-mode choices — never by hoping the client finds the money.`,
                    insight_lost:           `Lost the bid: a rival solved NorthGrid's problem better, cheaper, or faster. Re-examine where you designed before diagnosing, defaulted to bespoke or open, or failed to frame the pitch on the client's outcome. Pennine just forfeited 24% of its custom pipeline.`,
                    insight_marginbreach:   `Margin breached the 30% floor — the MD will not approve this bid. Every concession on days or price must buy something back, or it quietly converts a profitable mandate into a loss.`,
                    insight_faculty:        `Faculty over-allocation showed: spreading the 3 senior faculty across the whole design double-booked them and cannibalised £0.6m of open revenue. Reserve scarce faculty for the 2–3 moments only they can carry.`,
                    insight_launch:         `Launch readiness fell short of a credible 10-week cohort 1. With an anchor client, a late or under-rehearsed launch risks the relationship — a phased proof cohort hits the date without betting the mandate.`,
                    insight_lowfit:         `Client fit stayed low — the design drifted toward generic open content or an undiagnosed need. NorthGrid is buying a bespoke answer to its decarbonisation problem; fit is what wins the renewal, not just the bid.`,
                    insight_renewal:        `This is a renewable mandate: fit, a fundable margin and a deliverable 10-week launch moving together, with L3/L4 impact designed in. The reference that wins your next anchor client starts here.`,

                    hint_margin:            `Margin has slipped below the 30% floor — the MD won't approve it. Stop giving away days and price; trade concessions for scale or phase the commitment instead.`,
                    hint_budget:            `Your design still exceeds the £1.8m envelope. Close the gap with a hybrid spine and cheaper delivery modes, not by cutting the outcome NorthGrid is buying.`,
                    hint_fit:               `Client fit is weak — the design isn't yet answering NorthGrid's real need. Revisit the diagnosis (behaviour change, the CHRO buyer) and keep the relevant content custom.`,
                    hint_launch:            `Launch readiness is behind a credible 10-week cohort 1. Phase a proof cohort and lean on scalable virtual and digital modes to hit the date.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — fit, margin and win probability all healthy. Lock in the L3/L4 impact measurement and the phased launch so the win survives contact with procurement.`,

